There's the practical reality of their health concerns - the father's cough, the mother's arthritis - but that doesn't override what they're actually asking for. Moving out with the ability to help from a distance respects both their needs and their autonomy, and her parents' own words give her permission to do this.", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "```json
